  <data key="d5">In situ sulfur doping promotes surface reconstruction of NiFe LDH toward highly active S-doped oxyhydroxides; the sulfur-anion-induced effect lowers the reconstruction energy barrier, while the generated S-Ni_xFe_yOOH optimizes OER-intermediate adsorption and facilitates OER kinetics.</data>
  <data key="d6">surface-reconstruction mechanism</data>
  <data key="d7">In situ sulfur doping promotes surface reconstruction of NiFe LDH toward highly active S-doped oxyhydroxides; the sulfur-anion-induced effect lowers the reconstruction energy barrier, while the generated S-Ni_xFe_yOOH optimizes OER-intermediate adsorption and facilitates OER kinetics.</data>
  <data key="d8">mixed</data>
  <data key="d9">Mechanistic interpretation explicitly attributed to theoretical calculations, operando Raman, and ex situ characterizations.</data>
  <data key="d10">["claim_s_promotes_reconstruction_and_oer"]</data>
  <data key="d11">1</data>
  <data key="d12">broad_mechanism_abstract</data>
  <data key="d13">broad_abstract_support</data>
  <data key="d14">True</data>
  <data key="d15">abstract</data>
  <data key="d16">type: MechanismClaim
label: In situ sulfur doping promotes surface reconstruction of NiFe LDH toward highly active S-doped oxyhydroxides; the sulfur-anion-induced effect lowers the reconstruction energy barrier, while the generated S-Ni_xFe_yOOH optimizes OER-intermediate adsorption and facilitates OER kinetics.
source depth: abstract
epistemic use: exploration/bridge; verify before target-domain premise use
description: Mechanistic interpretation explicitly attributed to theoretical calculations, operando Raman, and ex situ characterizations.</data>
  <data key="d17">broad_372320cc91700e11f5d2</data>
  <data key="d18">claim_s_promotes_reconstruction_and_oer</data>
  <data key="d19">["broad_372320cc91700e11f5d2"]</data>
