<node id="paper::broad_444fa95d3a7db533ade0::claim_reconstruction_free">
  <data key="d4">MechanismClaim</data>
  <data key="d5">The strong atomic metal–support interaction in Ru/Ni3V-LDH stabilizes the dangling-bond-rich surface and reactive atomic Ru and Ni sites, enabling a steady dual-site configuration without surface reconstruction during HER/OER cycling.</data>
  <data key="d6">reconstruction-free bifunctional catalysis</data>
  <data key="d7">The strong atomic metal–support interaction in Ru/Ni3V-LDH stabilizes the dangling-bond-rich surface and reactive atomic Ru and Ni sites, enabling a steady dual-site configuration without surface reconstruction during HER/OER cycling.</data>
  <data key="d8">mixed</data>
  <data key="d9">The abstract attributes this interpretation to in situ X-ray absorption spectroscopy and operando Raman spectroscopy.</data>
  <data key="d10">["claim_reconstruction_free"]</data>
  <data key="d11">1</data>
  <data key="d12">broad_mechanism_abstract</data>
  <data key="d13">broad_abstract_support</data>
  <data key="d14">True</data>
  <data key="d15">abstract</data>
